# SYNTAX TEST "text.html.tiddlywiki5" "A verdict stands only where TiddlyWiki refuses"

# TiddlyWiki parses any tag name and any attribute name into a node — html.js accepts
# /<([a-zA-Z\-\$\.]+)/ and rejects only a leading dash. HTML deprecation says nothing about
# what TiddlyWiki builds, and the naming standard holds `invalid.deprecated` to "very rarely",
# so the tags and attributes HTML retired carry their ordinary names here.

! A tag HTML deprecated still builds a node

<center>x</center>
#^ entity.name.tag.html.tiddlywiki5
#^ - invalid.deprecated.html.tiddlywiki5

! A tag HTML dropped altogether still builds a node

<dir>z</dir>
#^ entity.name.tag.html.tiddlywiki5
#^ - invalid.illegal.no-longer-supported.html.tiddlywiki5

! An attribute HTML deprecated reads as an attribute name

<table align="left">y</table>
#      ^ entity.other.attribute-name.html.tiddlywiki5
#      ^ - invalid.deprecated.entity.other.attribute-name.html.tiddlywiki5

